--TEST--
`Core\Request\BodyStream::peek` gives `tainted bytes`, so a plain `bytes` variable does not compile, and its `max` is a `uint`, so a negative count does not compile — `rule:security/tainted-qualifier`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Request\BodyStream::peek
// The body comes from the client, so the start a peek reads is tainted.
Core\Request\BodyStream $body = Core\Request::bodyStream();
bytes $start = $body->peek(16);
tainted bytes $none = $body->peek(-1);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `bytes`, found `tainted bytes`
  --> case.nvs:5:16
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
